onald Trump arrived in Turkey on Tuesday to meet with fellow NATO leaders. The summit comes as the alliance tries to persuade him that their countries are actively increasing their military capabilities even as the American focus shifts away from its defense of Europe toward Asia. Read More 3 of 10 | President Donald Trump said the U.S. will lift sanctions on Turkey and consider restoring the sale of F-35 fighter jets to the country, signaling a possible reversal of a ban his administration imposed after Ankara bought Russian missile defense systems. Read More 4 of 10 | US President Donald Trump heads to Ankara, Turkey, on Monday evening for the annual NATO summit. Last year, he pushed alliance allies to spend more on defense. This year, his mission is to try to enforce those pledges. (AP Video: Nathan Ellgren) Read More 5 of 10 | Thousands of protestors from leftist parties, syndicates and women’s groups on Tuesday marched in central Istanbul against the NATO summit at the end of the first day of the conference. Read More 6 of 10 | NATO Secretary General Mark Rutte, center, poses with NATO defense ministers and industry representatives during the opening of the NATO Defense Industry Forum on the sidelines of the NATO summit in Ankara, Turkey, Tuesday, July 7, 2026. (AP Photo/Hussein Malla) License this photo Read More 7 of 10 | President Donald Trump shakes hands with Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan at the Bestepe Presidential Palace during a formal welcome for the NATO summit in Ankara, Turkey, Tuesday, July 7, 2026.(AP Photo/Alex Brandon) License this photo Read More 8 of 10 | Ukraine’s President Volodymyr Zelenskyy looks out from his car window as he arrives for the NATO summit in Ankara, Turkey, Tuesday, July 7, 2026. (Metin Aktaş, Pool Photo via AP) License this photo Read More 9 of 10 | Police detain protestors during a demonstration outside of the NATO summit in Ankara, Turkey, Tuesday, July 7, 2026. (AP Photo/Ali Unal) License this photo Read More 10