data/sources/coverage/cbs-21air-safety-record-2026-09-08.txt:6:The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) rejected Seuring's complaint over his alleged retaliatory firing by 21 Air. His appeal led to a 2023 Department of Labor tribunal — a hearing in front of a federal judge — where the case is still pending.
data/sources/coverage/cbs-21air-safety-record-2026-09-08.txt:8:Executives were accused of "paying lip service" to safety procedures "then doing exactly nothing," according to a resignation letter written by a former fighter pilot reviewing safety policy for the company and sent to 21 Air owner Crane in 2021.
data/sources/coverage/cbs-21air-safety-record-2026-09-08.txt:12:Mendez testified that Joseph "was fired from 21 Air and left under very bad circumstances" and that he believed the former chief pilot was trying to "make up" damaging claims.
data/sources/coverage/cbs-21air-safety-record-2026-09-08.txt:29:Retired 21 Air pilot Tony Bless, who testified in Seuring's case, told CBS News that for him, Sunday's crash in Miami did not come out of the blue.
