 his efforts to tame inflation and spur the US economy while speaking to the World Economic Forum. But his more than 70-minute address focused more on his gripes with other countries. Read More 3 of 10 | Greenland is the object of Trump’s desire, but he keeps calling it Iceland Read More 4 of 10 | President Donald Trump called for “immediate negotiations” for the U.S. to acquire Greenland from Denmark during his speech Wednesday at the World Economic Forum in Davos. But the president vowed he “won’t use force” to take over the island. Read More 5 of 10 | Keir Starmer made the comments in London on Wednesday, as tension between European nations and U.S. President Donald Trump continues to escalate over Trump’s insistence that the U.S. take ownership of Greenland. Read More 6 of 10 | President Donald Trump, right, meets with NATO Secretary General Mark Rutte during a meeting on the sidelines of the Annual Meeting of the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland, Wednesday, Jan. 21, 2026. (AP Photo/Evan Vucci) License this photo Read More 7 of 10 | President Donald Trump walks on to the stage during the 56th annual meeting of the World Economic Forum, WEF, in Davos, Switzerland, Wednesday, Jan. 21, 2026. (Gian Ehrenzeller/Keystone via AP) License this photo Read More 8 of 10 | President Donald Trump addresses the audience during the Annual Meeting of the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland, Wednesday, Jan. 21, 2026. (AP Photo/Evan Vucci) License this photo Read More 9 of 10 | President Donald Trump speaks during the 56th annual meeting of the World Economic Forum, WEF, in Davos, Switzerland, Wednesday, Jan. 21, 2026. (Gian Ehrenzeller/Keystone via AP) License this photo Read More 10 of 10 | President Donald Trump speaks during the 56th annual meeting of the World Economic Forum, WEF, in Davos, Switzerland, Wednesday, Jan. 21, 2026. (Gian Ehrenzeller/Keystone via AP) License this photo Read More Trump backs down on Greenland and cancels tariff threat after NATO 