inutes ago White House to host first press briefing in over 40 days Administration | 50 minutes ago No negotiations with Canada right now: US trade rep Business | 1 hour ago GOP senator ‘disappointed’ over departure of Army secretary who clashed with Hegseth Senate | 1 hour ago View all Load more Energy & Environment Trump administration unveils additional details in Venezuela oil deal Comments: by Rachel Frazin - 09/01/26 9:59 AM ET Comments: Link copied by Rachel Frazin - 09/01/26 9:59 AM ET Comments: Link copied Vice President Vance once again taking aim at Michigan Video Player is loading. Play Video Pause Skip Backward Skip Forward Unmute Current Time 0:07 / Duration 1:25 Loaded : 56.03% 0:07 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off Subtitles (en) , selected CC1 Captions Audio Track default , selected Quality 360p 720p 1080p Auto , selected Fullscreen Share This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Advertisement White House Headlines - September 1, 2026 Today's Top Stories - September 1, 2026 White House Headlines - September 1, 2026 Trending on The Hill - September 1, 2026 WRIC: Rural Health Funding DC Bureau: Trump Ballroom Advances as Iran War Drags DC Bureau: Data Centers Debate Vance calls El-Sayed 'very, very evil' Trump announces Medicaid drug pricing deals with 9 firms DOT to suspend driving schools associated with failed English proficiency tests 'We're going to hit them hard': Trump vows retaliation to Iranian strikes (WEB) WDCW: trump arch backed by NPS White House Headlines - September 1, 2026 NOW PLAYING White House Headlines - September 1, 2026 The Trump administration unveiled additional details Monday evening about its new oil deal with Venezuela. The administration said in a press release that the Pentagon’s Office of Strategic Capital will take a 35 percent equity stake in North American Blue Energy Partners, a private company that is Venezuela’s second-largest private oil producer. It added that the firm, which will now be partly owned by the U.S. government, was given a 100-year concession for Venezuelan oil fields that are estimated to contain about 65 billion barrels of oil — about 21 percent of Venezuela’s total estimated oil. The administration also said that the U.S. will get the right to purchase 20 percent of the oil that North American Blue Energy Partners unearths at the cost of production. It said that this oil can be used to fill the U.S.’s Strategic Petroleum Reserve, which both the Trump and Biden administrations have pulled from in recent years to mitigate the fuel price impacts of the war in Iran and Russia’s invasion of Ukraine. The State Department will also be given the first right of refusal to purchase the other 80 percent of the oil the company produces. The administration said that “millions of barrels” produced in Venezuela will be processed by U.S. refineries, but it did not specify a number or percentage. The new information comes as the initial details released by the administration were vague , saying the U.S. would work with a private operator but not naming the company. The Wall Street Journal reported that North American Blue Energy Partners is led by Alejandro Betancourt, who has faced investigations of alleged money laundering, though no charges have been filed. The Washington Post reported that the U.S. intervened in a Swiss criminal case against Betancourt, lobbying to avoid criminal charges and end travel restrictions against the businessman, who was based in the U.K. After the U.S. incursion into Venezuela at the start of the year, President Trump frequently said he wanted access to the country’s oil . Laura Kelly contributed. Add as preferred source on Google Tags Alejandro Betancourt Iran North American Blue Energy Partners Pentagon's Office of Strategic Capital russia state department strategic petroleum reserve Trump administration U.S. government Venezuela Venezuela Venezuela oil venezuelan oil Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. Comments: Link copied SPONSORED CONTENT Privacy Policy Privacy Policy Stage 3 Kidney Disease Doesn’t Have to End in Dialysis — Here’s the Upstream Support... The Metabolic Review | Sponsored Sponsored Read More Undo Halloween Lovers Are Obsessed With This 3D Rug Dayliy | Sponsored Sponsored Shop Now Undo The Worst Zip Codes for Car Insurance in Georgia (Is Yours on the List?) OTTO Insurance | Sponsored Sponsored Click Here Undo Seniors Above 55 Years Of Age Can Now Fly Business Class For The Price of Economy Smart Travel Tips | Sponsored Sponsored Learn More Undo Japan's Oldest Doctors Say Memory Loss Isn't Age: Just Avoid Drinking These 3 Beverages Matrix Ads 101 | Sponsored Sponsored Undo A Mayo Oncologist: Most Adults Over 50 Don't Need 12 Supplements Health Review | Sponsored Sponsored Undo Amazon Prime Membership Decline: Why Shoppers Canceling Prime For This? Online Shopping Tools | Sponsored Sponsored Learn More Undo Who Charges The Least For Car Insurance In Georgia? (Check Zip Codes) Many Georgia Drivers Had No Idea They Could Do This Auto Insurance | Sponsored Sponsored Learn more Undo Geo