checks/audits/jobs--2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000-2026-10-05-r9c-audit.log:4864:data/sources/coverage/ap-september-jobs.txt:31:At one time, 68,000 jobs a month would have been mediocre at best. But the United States doesn’t need as many jobs as it once did to keep unemployment from rising. Because of baby boomer retirements and Trump’s immigration crackdown, there are fewer people competing for work, and the break-even point could now be as low as zero jobs a month, down from 150,000 a year or two ago.
