checks/audits/greenland--september-2026-2026-09-09-zain-review.md:7:| 1 | Critical: the April €21.15 million may come from the existing €225 million envelope, so "€178.85 million remaining" is unsafe | Refuted. The pinned decision C(2026) 2542, Article 2, finances the €21.15 million from four lines of the general budget, E.14020240 to E.14020243, which the annex labels "NDICI Global Challenges" People, Planet, Prosperity, Partnerships (the four sum to 21,150,000.00). The legal basis is Regulation (EU) 2021/947, not Council Decision 2021/1764. The annex says the action "complements existing EU instruments deployed in Greenland, including the Green Growth Programme under the DOAG" and counts the DOAG green growth allocation (€22.5 million) as a separate instrument. | The page now states the budget lines and the instrument, says the money is not taken from the €225 million envelope, keeps the subtraction as a conditional ("if the whole €200 million is EU budget money"), and quotes "mobilising" with its ambiguity. Reviewer's hypothesis was wrong on the facts but right that the page had not shown its work. |
