checks/audits/jobs--2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000-2026-10-03-r1-editor.md:36:5. **Major · new · FIX.** “More people were working in September, and the labor force grew by more than employment did (485,000 against 406,000).” The first clause asserts the direction of the true change after the same paragraph acknowledges that the household estimate is below its significance bar. The [BLS pin](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/bls-empsit-2026-09.txt:454) gives “the household survey is about 650,000.” Its [household row](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/bls-empsit-2026-09.txt:336) ends “| 406 |”. Keep the estimated comparison; qualify the claim of what happened to actual employment.
checks/audits/jobs--2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000-2026-10-03-r1-editor.md:46:1. **Did the household survey establish that more people actually worked in September?** The [BLS pin](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/bls-empsit-2026-09.txt:454) gives “about 650,000” as the household significance threshold; its [employment row](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/bls-empsit-2026-09.txt:336) ends “| 406 |”. This changes **answer 3** and displaces the certainty in item 5.
checks/audits/jobs--2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000-2026-10-03-r2-redteam.md:3:2. **Major · new.** Page: “employment rose by 406,000 and the labor force by 485,000, both under that survey's bar of about 650,000.” The [pinned BLS FAQ](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/bls-empsit-2026-09.txt:448) gives that approximate bar for a household-survey **employment change**, not every household measure. BLS’s [September significance table](https://www.bls.gov/web/empsit/cpssigsuma.htm) gives separate exact rows: `Civilian labor force | 170,262 | 485 | 668 | No` and `Employed | 163,152 | 406 | 678 | No`. Neither estimate clears its own bar, but the page applies the employment bar to the labor force.
checks/audits/jobs--july-2026-2026-09-08.md:32:   - **Uncertainty bytes:** 18573-18786 says approximately 122,000 is required for statistical significance in the establishment survey and approximately 650,000 in the household employment survey. Bytes 36965-37149 say the two newest months use incomplete returns and are preliminary.
checks/audits/jobs--july-2026-2026-09-08.md:68:On September 4, later employer responses and recalculated seasonal factors revised July to plus 21,000. Revised July private payrolls rose 71,000 while government payrolls fell 50,000. August then added 162,000 jobs. Local government education added 42,000 in August, which BLS said largely offset the prior decrease. The labor force grew by 683,000, participation rose to 61.6 percent, and U-6 fell from 7.9 to 7.7 percent. These later observations disprove the article’s continued “reverse” framing and resolve its immediate labor-force-exit question in the opposite direction, while the three-month payroll average of about 71,000 still describes subdued growth.
checks/audits/missouri-house-map--september-2026-2026-09-08.md:13:| Other | 300,000 is a raw count; AG superlative untested | Yes: opinion "purporting to contain more than 300,000 signatures"; conceded points | Fixed: raw-versus-valid stated; superlative labeled as the attorney general's claim, not tested by us |
checks/audits/missouri-house-map--september-2026-2026-09-08.md:93:The “more than 300,000 signatures” figure is a raw-submission count, not a count of verified valid signatures. The court treated timeliness and minimum signatures as conceded because Hoskins omitted those objections from his certificate. [Missouri opinion](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site/data/sources/missouri-house-map/sc101805-opinion.txt:158)
checks/audits/missouri-house-map--september-2026-2026-09-08.md:158:Missouri Republicans enacted HB1 in September 2025 after President Trump urged mid-decade redistricting aimed at improving the party’s House position. Opponents pursued a referendum and submitted more than 300,000 raw signatures in December.

