checks/audits/jobs--august-2026-2026-09-08.md:78:**Correct account:** Restaurants and local education supplied 62 percent of the point-estimate gain, so growth was concentrated by magnitude. It was not narrowly confined to those industries. The official breadth measure improved to 55.6. Seasonal payback is a credible competing interpretation, not a demonstrated consensus, and the available sources provide no denominator for “not a minority view.”
checks/audits/jobs--august-2026-2026-09-08.md:100:Restaurants and local-government education contributed 101,000 of the point estimate, with seasonal effects plausibly explaining part of both movements. At the same time, the official diffusion index rose to 55.6, so gains were broader than the page’s payback framing conveys. Both facts belong in the account.
